WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.090
SO YOU'VE JUST HEARD WHY OUR
NOMINEES FOR ANIMATED SHORTS

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.700
FELL IN LOVE WITH ANIMATION.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.700
ME?

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.130
I FELL IN LOVE WITH ANIMATED MOVIES
WHEN MY MOTHER TOOK ME

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.110
TO A MOVIE THEATER FOR THE VERY
FIRST TIME TO SEE THE ANIMATED

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.460
MOVIE CALLED, 
"THE SECRET OF NIMH."

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.480
I REMEMBER VIVIDLY THE 
LEAD CHARACTER

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.480
WAS MRS. BRISBY

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.539
AND SHE WAS A FIERCE MOTHER 
MOUSE DETERMINED TO PROTECT HER

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:21.770
CHILDREN FROM A DANGEROUS
FARMER'S PLOW.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:27.270
IT WAS MY FIRST EXPERIENCE SEEING A
STRONG WOMAN AT THE CENTER OF A FILM.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.220
AND THAT IS THE POWER OF REALLY
GREAT ANIMATION.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.559
IT SHOWS YOU, AS A CHILD, THAT
ANYTHING IS POSSIBLE.

00:00:33.559 --> 00:00:38.460
THAT YOU CAN CHANGE THE WORLD,
EVEN IF YOU'RE AS SMALL AS A MOUSE.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.129
TONIGHT, WE HAVE NOMINEES
HERE WITH US IN PERSON,

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:44.629
BUT WE WANT TO SAY A SPECIAL HELLO
TO THOSE JOINING US

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:48.059
FROM LONDON AND
KILKENNY, IRELAND.

00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:52.176
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:00:52.176 --> 00:00:56.329
HERE ARE THE NOMINEES FOR BEST
ANIMATED FEATURE.

00:00:56.329 --> 00:00:59.429
"ONWARD,"
DAN SCANLON AND KORI RAE

00:00:59.429 --> 00:01:04.390
"OVER THE MOON," GLEN KEANE,
GENNIE RIM AND PEILIN CHOU

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.159
"A SHAUN THE SHEEP MOVIE:
FARMAGEDDON"

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:09.659
RICHARD PHELAN, WILL BECHER
AND PAUL KEWLEY

00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:13.370
"SOUL," PETE DOCTER
AND DANA MURRAY

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:14.370
"WOLFWALKERS"

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.080
TOMM MOORE, ROSS STEWART,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.603
PAUL YOUNG AND 
STEPHAN ROELANTS.

00:01:24.162 --> 00:01:30.516
AND THE OSCAR FOR BEST
ANIMATED FEATURE GOES TO --

00:01:30.516 --> 00:01:31.467
"SOUL."

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:35.425
PETE DOCTER AND
DANA MURRAY

00:01:35.425 --> 00:01:44.829
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.674
WOW. OKAY

00:01:52.674 --> 00:01:55.530
I'VE BEEN NOMINATED 
TO SPEAK ON BEHALF

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.900
OF DANA AND KEMP POWERS,
OUR CO-DIRECTOR.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:01.100
THIS FILM STARTED AS A LOVE
LETTER TO JAZZ,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.319
BUT WE HAD NO IDEA HOW MUCH
JAZZ WOULD TEACH US ABOUT LIFE.

00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:07.860
LIKE WE DON'T GET TO CONTROL
WHAT HAPPENS, BUT WE CAN,

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.690
LIKE A JAZZ MUSICIAN,
TURN WHATEVER HAPPENS INTO

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.860
SOMETHING OF VALUE AND
SOMETHING OF BEAUTY.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.980
AND THAT WAS CERTAINLY TRUE
OF OUR AMAZING CAST:

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.100
JAMIE FOXX, TINA FEY, YOU GUYS ARE AMAZING.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.040
OUR BRILLIANT COLLABORATORS
TRENT REZNOR AND ATTICUS ROSS,

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.210
JON BATISTE, THIS GUY OVER THERE.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:30.400
IT WAS JUST FANTASTIC, WORKING
WITH ALL YOU GUYS.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.580
OUR CULTURAL CONSULTANTS

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.130
DR. JOHNNETTA COLE.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.930
PEOPLE WHO KEPT US HONEST
AND KEEP THOSE CHARACTERS TRUTHFUL.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.970
WE'RE REALLY THANKFUL TO OUR
PARTNERS AT DISNEY WHO,

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.290
WHEN WE SAID, “HEY, WE WANT TO
DO A FILM THAT EXPLORES

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.040
THE PURPOSE OF LIFE,” THEY'RE LIKE,
“OKAY, GO AHEAD.”

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.540
THAT'S NOT YOUR USUAL 
CARTOON FARE.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.510
AND OF COURSE, TO OUR FAMILY.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.099
DANA WANTS TO THANK…

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:57.650
&gt;&gt; MY AMAZING HUSBAND, MY PARENTS.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.060
I'M HERE BECAUSE OF YOU.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.340
I LOVE YOU SO MUCH.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.250
HAZEL AND MURRAY, MY BABIES AT HOME.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.070
YOU'RE EVERYTHING TO ME.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.250
WE OBVIOUSLY HAVE TO THANK
THE CREW WHO MADE THIS FILM

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.730
AND EVEN FINISHED IT FROM HOME
WITH SEVEN WEEKS OF PRODUCTION LEFT.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:14.180
YOU ARE, YOU SHOULD BE UP
HERE WITH US,

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.340
AND WE ARE JUST THE 
LUCKY SPEAKERS.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:20.850
I'M NOT SUPPOSED TO BE 
SPEAKING ACTUALLY.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.700
&gt;&gt; SO OUR MAIN CHARACTER, JOE,
IS A MUSIC TEACHER.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.380
WE WANT TO THANK MUSIC TEACHERS
AND ART TEACHERS EVERYWHERE.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.590
YOU, INCLUDING MY PARENTS,
DAVE AND RITA, AND DANA'S PARENTS,

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:32.660
PAM AND TOM, YOU MAKE THE
WORLD A BETTER PLACE.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.800
AND MY WISH FOR ALL OF US TONIGHT
IS THAT WE COULD FOLLOW

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.410
THE EXAMPLE OF JAZZ MUSICIANS
THAT WHEREVER WE ARE,

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:43.280
WHATEVER WE HAVE,
WE TURN IT INTO SOMETHING BEAUTIFUL.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:43.780
THANK YOU.

